Answers to Player              NannyMUD Times                         Page 8
Question from March 2007

  March's question was:
  * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
      How and why did you choose your character name? 
      Would you change it now if you could?
  * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *

Lourdes:
  Once upon a time, I heard that the name Lourdes is one of the most
  difficult French/Spanish names to pronounce. For some reason, that
  useless bit of trivia stuck with me when it came time to choose a name.

Bayar:
  Well, my characters name is my RL name actually. I didnt knew which alias of
  mine to choose so i just gave out my name. And here I am :).
  If I would like to change it ? Maybe not. People are already used to this name,
  so why change it ?

Carrotj:
  There has always been something about me and carrots, I have called myself
  JCarrot and CarrotMan in the past! Looking at the other names, it might have
  been better to choose something more realistic.

Yachiru:
  I chose my characters name because this is my favorite character in "Bleach."
  Bleach, for those who don't know, is a Japanese anime. Yachiru Kusajishi is a
  Shinigami lieutenant of the 11th division. I would most definitely not change
  my character's name, Yachiru is the best!

Haldemar:
  Prince Haldemar of Haaken is one of the most famous NPC of the original
  Dungeons and Dragons setting. The original boxed rule, well before the
  (now outdated) Advanced Dungeons & Dragons, now evolved in 3rd edition
  D&D, had a wonderful world setting named Mystara, which unfortunately
  remained unsupported after the rule upgrade, and eventually disappeared
  completely. In its last years, Bruce heard wrote a storyline in
  Dragon Magazine named "The Voyage of the Princess Ark", running
  from issues 153 to 188. In this serie of article, he told the story of
  a very special, intelligent flying ship named Princess Ark and its crew,
  exploring part still unknown of the world with its captain,
  the alphatian wizard Prince Haldemar of Haaken.
  Adventures included finding a Hollow World at the center of the planet,
  flying to the Moon (including a second, invisible moon!) and jump in time,
  with a flavour that reminds a fantasy version of the exploring adventures
  of Star Trek: Enterprise.

  I am a very old player of Nannymud (started playing in 1992!). After wizzing,
  I got a few seconds, but I had the bad habit of never take any note
  of the areas I explored and puzzled I solved. With time, old areas were
  closed and new areas were opened, and my mental records of this world
  slowly faded.

  So I decided to start again; this time with a brand new notebook; pen, pencil,
  and the (impossible) plan of exploring everything again. Because of the
  huge task I had in front, for the first time of my life I had a decent name
  for my character: the only real Explorer, Haldemar, Prince of Haaken,
  Captain of the Princess Ark.

  This character wants to be a tribute to a wonderful setting, an interesting
  character, and a genius in his work, Bruce Heard; and a tribute to Nannymud
  and -finally- a way to thank both for the many, many, MANY hourse spent
  playing both games.

  Quoting the favourite sentence of Haldemar:
    "Do adventures ever truly end in NannyMUD?"

Annie:
  Because Annie is a good, sensible, down-to-earth name, for a good, sensible,
  down-to-earth woman! Want to make somethin' of it?
  
Qantaqa:
  I choose my name out of a book, the title of which slips my mind.
  I'm named after a wolf which was a less important, but prevolent, character.
  I'd only change my name if I had to. Otherwise, I rather like it.

Sscorpion:
  I've had this name for 3 years or more and chatted with many a high wiz, 
  and not one has said anything, why now, why you?

  I chose it because I didnt think ScorchedScorpion would
  be, that being one of my old Role Play characters, and no, I wouldnt
  change it, it's a great way to start a conversation :)

Duncanthrax:
  Duncanthrax was the first king in the Flathead Dynasty. He overthrew 
  Zilbo III, the last king of the Entharion Dynasty. His military conquests 
  were responsible for most of the territories controlled by Quendor. 
  He conquered the Westlands from 660-662 AE and defeated the Antharian 
  Armada at the Battle of Fort Griffspotter in 665 AE, gaining Quendor 
  control of the Great Sea. He build the castle at Egreth in 660 AE and 
  the seat of royal power would remain there until the rule of 
  Dimwit Flathead. In 666 AE, Duncanthrax further expanded Quendor with 
  the discovery of the underground caverns and an invasion of the Eastlands, 
  including the Diablo Massacre at Zorbel Pass and the decisive battle 
  of Globby Hills in which be buried the opposing army's champion orgre 
  in granola.

Fagarash:
  Well, i had friend in elementary school whose last name was Fagarash
  Why do you want me to change the name?

Ingwe:
  hmm, I don't think so, why?
  
Isobel:
  From the song Isobel by Bjork.

Amadeus:
