Liozar:
  My choice was irrational. It simply dawned on me after a
  great deal of thinking! And no, I don't want to ever change it.

Astrodeath:
  It was 1995 and I was listening to White Zombie's Astrocreep at the time.
  My first character's name was Astrocreep, but I forgot the password by the
  next time I tried to login, so I created Astrodeath. 

Vern:
  No, I wouldn't.
  
Belegur:
  I was reading Tolkien's _The Silmarillion_ at the time I
  created this character.  I wanted to use a name that wasn't well known.
  I would not change my name now if I could.

Polar:
  I don't remember why I chose this name, and I have other characters so
  I wouldn't change this one.
  
Kefka:
  Final Fantasy VI, because I was playing it for
  approximately 6 hours every day when I started on Nanny, and yes.
  
Beldin:
  I chose this handle when I was twelve because it had a
  similarity to my surname and because I liked David Eddings.  I used it
  when I was fifteen and started on NannyMUD.  Now, 13 years later, I
  don't think I would feel right changing it.

  But, I wouldn't choose it again.


  
